# 5. GAME MODES

Create seven distinct game modes.

### Mode 1 – Classic Maze

The main game mode.

- Navigate from start to finish.
- No time restrictions.
- No movement restrictions.
- Gradually increasing difficulty.
- Multiple maze geometries.
- Progressive level unlocking.

This should be the main progression experience.

### Mode 2 – Time Challenge

Complete the maze within a specified time limit.

- Different time limits depending on difficulty.
- Countdown display.
- Optional timer warning.
- Time-based scoring.
- Personal best records.
- Time Challenge leaderboard.

Award additional points for faster completion.

### Mode 3 – Restricted Moves

Complete the maze using a limited number of movements.

- Each valid movement consumes a move.
- Display remaining moves.
- Allow players to plan their route.
- Exceeding the movement allowance results in failure.
- Provide an option to restart.

Create progressively tighter movement allowances.

### Mode 4 – Token Collection

Collect all designated tokens before reaching the exit.

- Place collectible objects throughout the maze.
- Display the number of remaining tokens.
- Some tokens should require exploring alternative routes.
- All required tokens must be collected before the exit becomes active.
- Award bonus points for collecting every token.

Introduce different collectible designs and visual themes.

### Mode 5 – Intertwined Mazes

Introduce multiple interconnected maze sections.

- Two or more separate maze structures.
- Each maze has its own pathways.
- Teleportation portals connect designated locations.
- Players must identify which portal leads to the correct section.
- Some portals should provide alternative routes.
- Some should require additional exploration.

Display portal locations clearly while retaining the puzzle challenge.

### Mode 6 – Hidden Maze

An additional original gameplay mode.

- The maze begins partially or completely hidden.
- The player explores to reveal surrounding pathways.
- Previously explored sections remain visible.
- The exit is initially concealed.
- Include optional hints.

This mode should reward exploration and memory.

### Mode 7 – Mirror Maze

An additional original gameplay mode.

- Introduce mirrored or rotated maze sections.
- Movement through certain gateways transfers the player into a mirrored section.
- Some pathways correspond to different positions in another maze.
- Players must understand the relationship between connected sections.

Include increasingly challenging configurations.

